{
    "$schema": "../../schema/teletronix.schema.json",
    "config": {
        "name": "Teletronix Sample",
        "author": "@redhg",
        "description": "Demonstrates every Teletronix feature.",
        "start": "home"
    },
    "screens": {
        "home": {
            "content": [
                "TELETRONIX // SAMPLE PROGRAM",
                "============================",
                "",
                "Each line of a screen appears in turn. A bare string is a line of text. Long lines wrap at word boundaries to fit the window, so try resizing it.",
                "",
                "Click anywhere (except a link) to skip to the end of a screen.",
                "",
                { "type": "link", "text": "> TEXT", "action": { "screen": "text" } },
                { "type": "link", "text": "> REVEALS", "action": { "screen": "reveals" } },
                { "type": "link", "text": "> LINKS", "action": { "screen": "links" } },
                { "type": "link", "text": "> GLITCH", "action": { "screen": "glitch" } },
                { "type": "link", "text": "> TOGGLES", "action": { "screen": "toggles" } },
                { "type": "link", "text": "> PROMPT", "action": { "screen": "prompt" } },
                { "type": "link", "text": "> IMAGES", "action": { "screen": "images" } },
                { "type": "link", "text": "> DIALOGS", "action": { "screen": "dialogs" } },
                { "type": "link", "text": "> KEYS", "action": { "screen": "keys" } },
                { "type": "link", "text": "> PROGRESS", "action": { "screen": "progress" } },
                { "type": "link", "text": "> AUTOSCROLL", "action": { "screen": "autoscroll" } },
                { "type": "link", "text": "> EFFECTS", "action": { "screen": "effects" } }
            ]
        },
        "effects": {
            "content": [
                "EFFECTS",
                "=======",
                "",
                "Scanlines are on by default. \"effects\" in the config turns effects on or off and tunes them, and each screen can override that. Each of these screens turns one on:",
                "",
                { "type": "link", "text": "> STATIC", "action": { "screen": "fx-static" } },
                { "type": "link", "text": "> BLOOM", "action": { "screen": "fx-bloom" } },
                { "type": "link", "text": "> VIGNETTE", "action": { "screen": "fx-vignette" } },
                { "type": "link", "text": "> FLICKER", "action": { "screen": "fx-flicker" } },
                { "type": "link", "text": "> FRINGE", "action": { "screen": "fx-fringe" } },
                { "type": "link", "text": "> EVERYTHING", "action": { "screen": "fx-all" } },
                { "type": "link", "text": "> NO SCANLINES", "action": { "screen": "fx-clean" } },
                "",
                "Phosphor afterglow is a screen transition: the old screen fades out behind the new one.",
                { "type": "link", "text": "> AFTERGLOW", "action": { "screen": "fx-afterglow" } },
                "",
                "A static transition flashes noise between screens, like changing channels:",
                { "type": "link", "text": "> CHANGE CHANNEL", "action": { "screen": "fx-channel" } },
                "",
                "A screen can be nothing but effects, and \"next\" moves on without a link:",
                { "type": "link", "text": "> SIGNAL LOST", "action": { "screen": "fx-noise" } },
                "",
                { "type": "link", "text": "> BACK", "action": { "screen": "home" } }
            ]
        },
        "fx-channel": {
            "transition": "static",
            "content": [
                "CHANNEL 3",
                "=========",
                "",
                "This screen sets \"transition\": \"static\": a 120ms burst of noise before it appears. Set a \"duration\" to change it.",
                "",
                { "type": "link", "text": "> BACK", "action": { "screen": "effects" } }
            ]
        },
        "fx-noise": {
            "effects": { "static": { "opacity": 1, "scale": 2 } },
            "next": { "after": 1500, "action": { "screen": "fx-restored" } },
            "content": []
        },
        "fx-restored": {
            "reveal": "glitch",
            "next": { "key": "any", "action": { "screen": "effects" } },
            "content": [
                { "type": "text", "text": "SIGNAL RESTORED.", "className": "alert" },
                "",
                "The static screen had no content and \"next\": { \"after\": 1500, ... }.",
                "",
                "This one has \"next\": { \"key\": \"any\", ... }. Press any key or click to continue."
            ]
        },
        "fx-static": {
            "effects": { "static": { "opacity": 0.25 } },
            "content": [
                "STATIC",
                "======",
                "",
                "Analog TV noise. Options: opacity, fps, scale.",
                "",
                { "type": "link", "text": "> BACK", "action": { "screen": "effects" } }
            ]
        },
        "fx-bloom": {
            "effects": { "bloom": true },
            "content": [
                "BLOOM",
                "=====",
                "",
                "Bright text and images glow into the dark around them. Options: strength, radius.",
                "",
                { "type": "link", "text": "> BACK", "action": { "screen": "effects" } }
            ]
        },
        "fx-vignette": {
            "effects": { "vignette": true },
            "content": [
                "VIGNETTE",
                "========",
                "",
                "The corners of the screen darken, like the edge of a tube. Option: strength.",
                "",
                { "type": "link", "text": "> BACK", "action": { "screen": "effects" } }
            ]
        },
        "fx-flicker": {
            "effects": { "flicker": true },
            "content": [
                "FLICKER",
                "=======",
                "",
                "The picture dims by small, irregular amounts. Option: strength.",
                "",
                { "type": "link", "text": "> BACK", "action": { "screen": "effects" } }
            ]
        },
        "fx-fringe": {
            "effects": { "fringe": { "offset": 1.5 } },
            "content": [
                "FRINGE",
                "======",
                "",
                "Red and cyan fringes on the text, like misaligned color guns. Options: offset, strength.",
                "",
                { "type": "link", "text": "> BACK", "action": { "screen": "effects" } }
            ]
        },
        "fx-all": {
            "effects": { "bloom": true, "vignette": true, "flicker": { "strength": 0.3 }, "static": { "opacity": 0.1 }, "fringe": true },
            "content": [
                "EVERYTHING",
                "==========",
                "",
                "Every effect at once.",
                "",
                { "type": "link", "text": "> BACK", "action": { "screen": "effects" } }
            ]
        },
        "fx-clean": {
            "effects": { "scanlines": false },
            "content": [
                "NO SCANLINES",
                "============",
                "",
                "This screen turns the scanlines off.",
                "",
                { "type": "link", "text": "> BACK", "action": { "screen": "effects" } }
            ]
        },
        "fx-afterglow": {
            "transition": { "type": "fade", "duration": 1500 },
            "content": [
                "AFTERGLOW",
                "=========",
                "",
                "This screen sets \"transition\": { \"type\": \"fade\", \"duration\": 1500 }, so the screen you came from faded out slowly behind it.",
                "",
                { "type": "link", "text": "> BACK", "action": { "screen": "effects" } }
            ]
        },
        "dialogs": {
            "content": [
                "DIALOGS",
                "=======",
                "",
                "Links and commands can open dialogs. An alert closes with <enter>, <esc> or a click:",
                { "type": "link", "text": "> SHOW ALERT", "action": { "dialog": "hello" } },
                "",
                "A confirm dialog asks a question, and each answer can do something:",
                { "type": "link", "text": "> SELF-DESTRUCT", "className": "alert", "action": { "dialog": "destruct" } },
                "",
                { "type": "link", "text": "> BACK", "action": { "screen": "home" } }
            ]
        },
        "progress": {
            "content": [
                "PROGRESS",
                "========",
                "",
                "A bar runs from one value to another over a set time, then the screen carries on. It can run backwards, and hide its value:",
                "",
                { "type": "progress", "label": "DOWNLOADING  ", "duration": 2500 },
                { "type": "progress", "label": "SHIELDS      ", "from": 77, "to": 0, "duration": 2000, "className": "alert" },
                { "type": "progress", "label": "CALIBRATING  ", "from": 54, "to": 75, "percent": false, "fill": "#", "empty": ".", "duration": 1500 },
                "",
                "It can fail partway:",
                "",
                {
                    "type": "progress",
                    "label": "TRANSFER     ",
                    "duration": 3000,
                    "interrupt": { "at": 73, "text": "INTERRUPTED" },
                    "className": "alert"
                },
                "",
                "Or do something when it's done. This one uploads, and you can abort it with <esc>:",
                { "type": "link", "text": "> UPLOAD LOGS", "action": { "screen": "upload" } },
                { "type": "link", "text": "> BACK", "action": { "screen": "home" } }
            ]
        },
        "upload": {
            "content": [
                "UPLOADING STATION LOGS. PRESS <ESC> TO ABORT.",
                "",
                {
                    "type": "progress",
                    "label": "UPLOAD  ",
                    "duration": 5000,
                    "onComplete": { "after": 600, "action": { "screen": "upload-done" } },
                    "interrupt": { "key": "Escape", "text": "ABORTED", "after": 800, "action": { "screen": "progress" } }
                }
            ]
        },
        "upload-done": {
            "next": { "key": "any", "action": { "screen": "progress" } },
            "content": ["UPLOAD COMPLETE.", "", "Press any key."]
        },
        "autoscroll": {
            "reveal": { "type": "teletype", "speed": 4 },
            "content": [
                "AUTOSCROLL",
                "==========",
                "",
                "When a screen is taller than the window, it scrolls to keep the newest text in view. Scroll up to reread and it stops following; scroll back down and it picks up again. Set \"autoscroll\": false in the config or on a screen to turn it off.",
                "",
                "0001  CRYO BAY       OK",
                "0002  LIFE SUPPORT   NOMINAL",
                "0003  REACTOR        NOMINAL",
                "0004  LIFE SUPPORT   OK",
                "0005  LIFE SUPPORT   OK",
                "0006  CARGO LIFT     OK",
                "0007  REACTOR        OK",
                "0008  LIFE SUPPORT   OK",
                "0009  HYDROPONICS    NOMINAL",
                "0010  HYDROPONICS    OK",
                "0011  HULL SENSORS   NOMINAL",
                "0012  COMMS ARRAY    OK",
                "0013  COMMS ARRAY    OK",
                "0014  HYDROPONICS    NOMINAL",
                "0015  COMMS ARRAY    NOMINAL",
                "0016  HYDROPONICS    OK",
                "0017  REACTOR        WARN: DRIFT 0.9%",
                "0018  REACTOR        NOMINAL",
                "0019  HULL SENSORS   WARN: DRIFT 0.8%",
                "0020  AIRLOCK 2      OK",
                "0021  AIRLOCK 1      OK",
                "0022  NAV COMPUTER   OK",
                "0023  HULL SENSORS   NOMINAL",
                "0024  NAV COMPUTER   OK",
                "0025  CRYO BAY       OK",
                "0026  HYDROPONICS    OK",
                "0027  AIRLOCK 2      OK",
                "0028  CRYO BAY       OK",
                "0029  CARGO LIFT     WARN: DRIFT 0.1%",
                "0030  REACTOR        NOMINAL",
                "0031  CRYO BAY       WARN: DRIFT 0.6%",
                "0032  CRYO BAY       NOMINAL",
                "0033  AIRLOCK 1      OK",
                "0034  NAV COMPUTER   WARN: DRIFT 0.8%",
                "0035  REACTOR        WARN: DRIFT 0.1%",
                "0036  NAV COMPUTER   OK",
                "0037  CARGO LIFT     OK",
                "0038  AIRLOCK 1      OK",
                "0039  HYDROPONICS    OK",
                "0040  LIFE SUPPORT   OK",
                "",
                "END OF LOG.",
                { "type": "link", "text": "> BACK", "action": { "screen": "home" } }
            ]
        },
        "keys": {
            "next": [
                { "key": "y", "action": { "screen": "destroyed" } },
                { "key": ["n", "Escape"], "action": { "screen": "home" } },
                { "after": 10000, "action": { "screen": "keys-timeout" } }
            ],
            "content": [
                "KEYS",
                "====",
                "",
                "A screen's \"next\" can list rules, and the first to trigger wins. This one has three: Y, N (or Esc), and a 10 second timeout.",
                "",
                { "type": "text", "text": "INITIATE SELF-DESTRUCT? [Y/N]", "className": "alert" }
            ]
        },
        "keys-timeout": {
            "next": { "key": "any", "action": { "screen": "home" } },
            "content": ["No answer. Self-destruct cancelled.", "", "Press any key."]
        },
        "destroyed": {
            "transition": "glitch",
            "reveal": "glitch",
            "content": [
                { "type": "text", "text": "SELF-DESTRUCT SEQUENCE INITIATED.", "className": "alert" },
                "",
                "Just kidding.",
                "",
                { "type": "link", "text": "> BACK", "action": { "screen": "dialogs" } }
            ]
        },
        "toggles": {
            "content": [
                "TOGGLES",
                "=======",
                "",
                "A toggle cycles through its states each time you click it. Toggles remember their state, so leave this screen and come back.",
                "",
                { "type": "toggle", "states": ["> Hello.", "> How are you?", "> I am fine, thanks."] },
                { "type": "toggle", "states": ["[ ] AIRLOCK SEALED", "[X] AIRLOCK SEALED"], "initial": 1, "className": "alert" },
                "",
                { "type": "link", "text": "> BACK", "action": { "screen": "home" } }
            ]
        },
        "prompt": {
            "content": [
                "PROMPT",
                "======",
                "",
                "Type a command and press <enter>. Commands ignore case and extra spaces. Try:",
                "",
                "  HOME     back to the start",
                "  GLITCH   the glitch demo",
                "  IMAGES   (or PICS) the image demo",
                "  HELP     (or ?) a dialog",
                "",
                {
                    "type": "prompt",
                    "prompt": "Enter command: ",
                    "unknown": "Unknown command. Try HOME, GLITCH, IMAGES or HELP.",
                    "commands": [
                        { "command": "home", "action": { "screen": "home" } },
                        { "command": "glitch", "action": { "screen": "glitch" } },
                        { "command": ["images", "pics"], "action": { "screen": "images" } },
                        { "command": ["help", "?"], "action": { "dialog": "help" } }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        "images": {
            "content": [
                "IMAGES",
                "======",
                "",
                "A bitmap loads, then resolves from blocky to sharp. The screen waits for it to load.",
                { "type": "bitmap", "src": "data/images/sunset-grid.png", "alt": "A striped sun setting over a neon grid" },
                "",
                "\"blend\" blends an image with the screen's background color. Against a dark screen, these three stand out.",
                "",
                "\"luminosity\": a monochrome, tinted to the screen:",
                { "type": "bitmap", "src": "data/images/sunset-grid.png", "alt": "The sunset in monochrome, tinted to the screen color", "blend": "luminosity" },
                "",
                "\"hard-light\": bright parts burn, dark parts sink:",
                { "type": "bitmap", "src": "data/images/sunset-grid.png", "alt": "The sunset with a burning red sun over a darkened sky", "blend": "hard-light" },
                "",
                "\"overlay\": a faint ghost of the image:",
                { "type": "bitmap", "src": "data/images/sunset-grid.png", "alt": "A faint, dim ghost of the sunset", "blend": "overlay" },
                "",
                "Or blend with the text color: { \"mode\": \"luminosity\", \"with\": \"text\" } for an image in the screen's own color...",
                { "type": "bitmap", "src": "data/images/sunset-grid.png", "alt": "The sunset in the screen's text color", "blend": { "mode": "luminosity", "with": "text" } },
                "",
                "...or \"difference\" for a negative:",
                { "type": "bitmap", "src": "data/images/sunset-grid.png", "alt": "A photographic negative of the sunset", "blend": { "mode": "difference", "with": "text" } },
                "",
                { "type": "link", "text": "> BACK", "action": { "screen": "home" } }
            ]
        },
        "text": {
            "content": [
                "TEXT",
                "====",
                "",
                "A string can contain\nline breaks.",
                "",
                "An empty string makes a blank line, like the one above.",
                { "type": "text", "text": "Text objects can add CSS classes, like \"alert\".", "className": "alert" },
                "",
                { "type": "link", "text": "> BACK", "action": { "screen": "home" } }
            ]
        },
        "reveals": {
            "content": [
                "REVEALS",
                "=======",
                "",
                "By default, text teletypes in at 10ms per character.",
                { "type": "text", "text": "Any element can change its speed...", "reveal": { "type": "teletype", "speed": 60 } },
                { "type": "text", "text": "...or appear all at once.", "reveal": "instant" },
                "Screens and the config can set defaults too: the next screen shows everything instantly.",
                "",
                { "type": "link", "text": "> INSTANT SCREEN", "action": { "screen": "instant" } },
                { "type": "link", "text": "> BACK", "action": { "screen": "home" } }
            ]
        },
        "instant": {
            "reveal": "instant",
            "content": [
                "INSTANT",
                "=======",
                "",
                "This screen sets \"reveal\": \"instant\", so its elements appear at once...",
                { "type": "text", "text": "...unless an element overrides it, like this one.", "reveal": "teletype" },
                "",
                { "type": "link", "text": "> BACK", "action": { "screen": "reveals" } }
            ]
        },
        "links": {
            "content": [
                "LINKS",
                "=====",
                "",
                "A link that points to the current screen replays it:",
                { "type": "link", "text": "> REPLAY THIS SCREEN", "action": { "screen": "links" } },
                "",
                "Links can do something different when shift-clicked. This one shows an alert, but shift-click it to find a hidden screen:",
                {
                    "type": "link",
                    "text": "> LOCKED. Shift+click to unlock",
                    "className": "alert",
                    "action": { "dialog": "locked" },
                    "shiftAction": { "screen": "secret" }
                },
                "",
                { "type": "link", "text": "> BACK", "action": { "screen": "home" } }
            ]
        },
        "glitch": {
            "reveal": "glitch",
            "transition": "glitch",
            "content": [
                "GLITCH",
                "======",
                "",
                "This screen sets \"reveal\": \"glitch\", so its text resolves out of random glyphs. When a screen (or the config) sets it, consecutive elements glitch in together as one block.",
                "",
                "It also sets \"transition\": \"glitch\", so the screen you came from erased itself over this one as it appeared.",
                "",
                { "type": "text", "text": "An element can set its own glitch, which runs by itself, like this slow one.", "reveal": { "type": "glitch", "duration": 3000 } },
                "",
                { "type": "link", "text": "> NEXT PAGE", "action": { "screen": "glitch2" } },
                { "type": "link", "text": "> BACK", "action": { "screen": "home" } }
            ]
        },
        "glitch2": {
            "reveal": "glitch",
            "transition": { "type": "glitch", "duration": 1500 },
            "content": [
                "TELETRONIX // SYSTEM LOG",
                "",
                "> Connection established. Signal integrity at 73%. Stand by for transmission from the outer relay.",
                { "type": "text", "text": "> WARNING: hull breach detected on deck 4. Crew manifest incomplete. Two life signs unaccounted for.", "className": "alert" },
                "> Awaiting operator input_",
                "",
                { "type": "link", "text": "> PREVIOUS PAGE", "action": { "screen": "glitch" } },
                { "type": "link", "text": "> BACK", "action": { "screen": "home" } }
            ]
        },
        "secret": {
            "content": [
                { "type": "text", "text": "ACCESS GRANTED", "className": "alert" },
                "",
                { "type": "link", "text": "> BACK", "action": { "screen": "links" } }
            ]
        }
    },
    "dialogs": {
        "hello": {
            "type": "alert",
            "content": ["This is an alert.", "", "Press <enter>, <esc>, or click anywhere to close it."]
        },
        "locked": {
            "type": "alert",
            "className": "alert",
            "content": "This link is locked. You'll need to <shift>+click it.",
            "dismiss": "UNDERSTOOD"
        },
        "help": {
            "type": "alert",
            "content": "Commands: HOME, GLITCH, IMAGES (or PICS), HELP (or ?)."
        },
        "destruct": {
            "type": "confirm",
            "className": "alert",
            "content": ["Initiate the station self-destruct sequence?", "", "This cannot be undone."],
            "confirm": { "text": "CONFIRM", "action": { "screen": "destroyed" } },
            "cancel": { "text": "ABORT", "action": { "dialog": "aborted" } }
        },
        "aborted": {
            "type": "alert",
            "content": "Self-destruct aborted."
        }
    }
}
